---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalDoc from '~/components/widgets/LegalDoc.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '~/config/contact';
import { site, siteHost } from '~/config/site';

const host = siteHost();
const legalName = CONTACT.businessName;
const dbaName = site.name;
const entityLabel = legalName === dbaName ? legalName : `${legalName} (doing business as ${dbaName})`;
const governingState = CONTACT.address.state === 'HI' ? 'Hawaii' : CONTACT.address.state;
const governingCounty = 'Honolulu';

const metadata = {
  title: `Terms of Service | ${dbaName}`,
  description: `Terms of Service for ${host}. These terms govern your use of the website and participation in ${dbaName} chapters, sessions, and activities.`,
  ignoreTitleTemplate: true,
};

const headingClass = 'text-h4 font-heading font-normal text-heading mb-4';
const bodyClass = 'text-body-lg font-normal leading-[160%] text-muted';
const listClass = `${bodyClass} mt-4 space-y-1 list-disc pl-5`;
const linkClass = 'btn-link';
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <Fragment slot="header"></Fragment>
  <LegalDoc title="Terms of Service">
    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>1. Acceptance of these terms</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        These Terms of Service govern your use of {host} and your participation in {dbaName} chapters, sessions, and activities.
        They are provided by {entityLabel}, referred to here as "we," "us," or "our." By accessing this website or
        taking part in any {dbaName} activity, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the site or
        take part in our activities.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>2. About {dbaName}</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        {dbaName} is a network of member-led chapters that offers in-person activities, educational sessions, books, and a
        self-assessment focused on healthy aging. Using this website, submitting a form, or attending a session does not by
        itself create a membership, a service agreement, or any other relationship beyond what these terms describe. Any membership
        terms, dues, or chapter agreements are provided to you separately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>3. Use of this website</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        You may use this website for lawful purposes, to learn about {dbaName}, and to inquire about or take part in our
        activities. You agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul class={listClass}>
        <li>Use the site in a way that violates any applicable law or regulation</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to the site, its servers, or any connected systems</li>
        <li>Introduce malware, or interfere with the normal operation or security of the site</li>
        <li>Copy, scrape, or republish site content for commercial purposes without our written permission</li>
        <li>
          Submit false, misleading, or fraudulent information through any form on the site, including first-visit
          bookings and chapter applications
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        We may restrict or suspend access to the site at any time, without notice, if we reasonably believe use of the
        site breaches these terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>4. Not medical advice</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        {dbaName} does not provide medical care. The content on this website, in our books and podcasts, and at our lectures,
        journal clubs, and chapter sessions is general educational information. It is not medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment,
        and it is not a substitute for care from a qualified health professional who knows your history.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        No doctor-patient or other professional relationship is created between you and {dbaName}, Dr. Robert Peterson,
        any lecturer, coach, chapter lead, or volunteer through your use of this website or your participation in our
        activities. Information about tests, screenings, supplements, or medications is provided so you can discuss it
        with your own physician. Do not start, stop, or change any medication or treatment based on anything you read or
        hear through {dbaName} without first speaking to your physician.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        Always seek the advice of your physician with any question about a medical condition, and never disregard
        professional medical advice or delay seeking it because of something you read or heard through {dbaName}. If you
        think you may have a medical emergency, call 911 or your local emergency number immediately.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>5. The self-assessment</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        The self-assessment on this website is an educational tool. It is not a medical test, a diagnosis, or a
        substitute for an examination by a health professional. Its results depend entirely on the answers you give, are
        not reviewed by any person, and may not reflect your actual health. Do not rely on your results to make medical
        decisions without speaking to your physician.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        The self-assessment is sponsored by Athena Clinic. How the self-assessment handles your answers is described in
        our
        <a class={linkClass} href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>6. Athena Clinic and disclosure of interest</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Athena Clinic is a separate medical practice owned by Dr. Robert Peterson, who is also the founder of{' '}
        {dbaName}. Athena Clinic sponsors the self-assessment, and this website links to services offered by Athena
        Clinic. Dr. Peterson has a financial interest in Athena Clinic. You are never required to use Athena Clinic to
        take part in {dbaName}, and the information on this website can be used with any physician you choose.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        Any assessment, session, consultation, package, test, or other service provided by Athena Clinic is offered
        solely by Athena Clinic, under its own terms, patient policies, and privacy practices, and not by us. Athena
        Clinic alone decides which of its services, if any, are offered at no charge, who is eligible, what is included,
        and what fees apply. Any mention on this website of an Athena Clinic service or offer, including one described
        as free or complimentary, is general information only, may change or end at any time without notice, and does
        not create a commitment by us.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        Before booking, confirm directly with Athena Clinic what a service includes, whether any charge applies, and
        whether your insurance covers it. We are not responsible for Athena Clinic's services, fees, billing, insurance
        determinations, scheduling, or any other matter between you and Athena Clinic.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>7. Chapters, sessions, and activities</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        {dbaName} chapters are run largely by members and volunteers. Session schedules, locations, leaders, speakers, and
        formats may change or be cancelled at any time, including because of weather, ocean conditions, or venue availability.
        Any offer of free visits applies as described on the relevant chapter page and may be limited by capacity, or changed
        or withdrawn at any time.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        Before you take part in certain activities, you may be asked to sign a participation agreement, release, or
        acknowledgment of risk. That document applies in addition to these terms. We may decline, limit, or end anyone's
        participation in any activity or chapter where we reasonably believe it is necessary for the safety or wellbeing
        of that person or others, or where these terms have been breached.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>8. Your health and your participation</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Many {dbaName} activities are physical, including strength training, balance and mobility work, walking, hiking, ocean
        swimming, yoga, and volunteer work. Physical activity carries inherent risks, including falls, muscle and joint injuries,
        heat illness, dehydration, strong currents and other ocean hazards, uneven terrain, cardiac events, and in rare cases
        serious injury or death. These risks exist even when activities are led carefully.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>By taking part, you agree that:</p>
      <ul class={listClass}>
        <li>
          You will talk to your physician before starting any new exercise or activity, particularly if you have a
          medical condition, take medication, or have recently been ill or injured
        </li>
        <li>
          Your participation is voluntary, and you are responsible for deciding whether an activity is suitable for you
        </li>
        <li>
          You will take part within your own abilities, use modified versions of exercises where you need them, and stop
          immediately if you feel pain, dizziness, shortness of breath, or discomfort
        </li>
        <li>
          You will tell the session leader about anything that could affect your safety, to the extent you are
          comfortable doing so
        </li>
        <li>
          You are responsible for assessing trail, weather, and ocean conditions for yourself, and ocean activities are
          not supervised by lifeguards unless a session description clearly states otherwise
        </li>
        <li>
          Coaches, chapter leads, and volunteers are not providing medical care and are not responsible for monitoring
          your health
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, you knowingly assume the risks of taking part in {dbaName}
        {' '}activities.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>9. Food at gatherings</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Food at kitchen salons, potlucks, and other gatherings may be prepared by members, volunteers, or guests,
        including in home kitchens. We cannot guarantee how any food was prepared, what it contains, or that it is free
        of allergens such as nuts, shellfish, dairy, gluten, or eggs. If you have a food allergy or dietary restriction,
        you are responsible for deciding what is safe for you to eat. Information about nutrition is general education
        and is not individual dietary advice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>10. Volunteer and service activities</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Some chapters take part in service activities organized with or by third parties, such as beach cleanups and
        meal delivery programs. Those organizations may have their own requirements, rules, and waivers, which you agree
        to follow. We are not responsible for the acts, omissions, or policies of those organizations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>11. Community conduct</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        {dbaName} depends on members treating each other with respect. When you take part in any chapter, session, or online
        space connected to {dbaName}, you agree not to:
      </p>
      <ul class={listClass}>
        <li>Harass, threaten, demean, or discriminate against any member, guest, volunteer, or speaker</li>
        <li>Share personal or health information another person has shared in a session without their permission</li>
        <li>Sell, promote, or solicit products, services, or investments to members</li>
        <li>
          Present yourself as giving professional medical, legal, or financial advice unless you are appropriately
          licensed and the setting clearly allows it
        </li>
        <li>Attend while impaired in a way that puts yourself or others at risk</li>
      </ul>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        We and our chapter leads may remove anyone from a session, chapter, or online space for conduct that breaches
        these terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>12. Photographs and recordings</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Sessions, lectures, and gatherings may be photographed, filmed, or recorded, and those materials may be used on
        this website, in podcasts, and in other {dbaName} materials. If you do not want to appear in photographs or recordings,
        tell the session leader before the session begins, and we will make reasonable efforts to respect your request. Where
        required, we will ask for your permission before featuring you by name.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>13. Lectures and educational content</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Lecturers, moderators, and guest speakers are independent. Their views are their own and do not necessarily
        reflect ours. References to research, trials, and published studies are provided for education and discussion,
        and research findings may not apply to your individual circumstances. Session summaries and recordings may be
        edited for length and clarity.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>14. Starting a chapter</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Submitting an application or inquiry about starting a chapter does not create a chapter, an affiliation, a
        partnership, or any right to use the {dbaName} name, materials, or support. A chapter is established only under a
        separate written agreement signed by us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>15. Membership and dues</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Where a chapter charges membership dues, the amount, frequency, and payment method will be disclosed to you
        before you join. If dues renew automatically, we will tell you before you join and you may cancel at any time
        using the method described in your membership terms, effective at the end of the current period. Except where
        stated in your membership terms or required by law, dues already paid are not refundable.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>16. Books and other products</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Books and related products may be sold through third-party publishers and retailers, including Lulu. Purchases
        made through those services are governed by their terms, including their pricing, payment, shipping, and return
        policies, and we are not responsible for their fulfillment. Where we sell products directly, the price,
        availability, and any shipping and return terms will be shown before you complete your purchase. Product
        descriptions are general and may contain errors, and prices and availability may change without notice.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>17. Forms and submissions</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        When you submit a form on this website, such as a first-visit booking, a waitlist request, a chapter
        application, or a general inquiry, you are asking us to contact you, and you agree that we or the relevant
        chapter lead may respond by email, phone, or text using the details you provide. Please do not submit detailed
        medical information, medical records, payment details, or confidential documents through the site. Information
        you send us is handled as described in our
        <a class={linkClass} href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>18. Text messages</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        If you provide a mobile number and opt in, we or your chapter may send text messages about your inquiry, visit,
        or chapter activities. Message and data rates may apply, and message frequency varies. Reply STOP to any message
        to opt out, or HELP for assistance. Consent to receive text messages is not a condition of joining a chapter or
        making any purchase.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>19. Third-party links and embedded content</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        This website may link to, or embed content from, third-party services such as Athena Clinic, publishers and
        retailers, podcast platforms, maps, and video services. We do not control those services and are not responsible
        for their content, availability, accuracy, fees, or privacy practices. Your use of a third-party service is
        governed by that provider's own terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>20. Cookies</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        This website may use cookies and similar technologies to operate the site and understand how it is used. You can
        control cookies through your browser settings. See our
        <a class={linkClass} href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for more detail, including how the self-assessment
        is handled.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>21. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Unless stated otherwise, the content on this website and in {dbaName} materials, including text, frameworks, the self-assessment,
        images, graphics, recordings, layout, and design, is owned by {legalName}, Dr. Robert Peterson, or our
        licensors, and is protected by copyright and other intellectual property laws. You may view, print, and save
        pages and your own self-assessment results for personal, non-commercial use. You may not reproduce, distribute,
        modify, sell, or create derivative works from this content, or use it to run programs, classes, or groups of
        your own, without our written permission.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        Third-party names, trademarks, and logos, including those of research institutions, publishers, and service
        organizations, remain the property of their respective owners and are used only to identify them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>22. Copyright complaints</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        If you believe content on this website infringes your copyright, contact us
        with a description of the work, the location of the material on our site, your contact details, a statement that you
        believe the use is unauthorized, and a statement that the information in your notice is accurate. We will review the
        notice and remove or disable access to the material where appropriate. If material of yours was removed in error,
        you may contact us at the same address to respond.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>23. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, this website, its content, the self-assessment, and all{' '}
        {dbaName} activities are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis, without warranties of any kind, whether
        express or implied, including implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
        We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted, secure, or free of errors, or that any information is complete,
        accurate, or current.
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        We make no promise of any health outcome. Member stories and testimonials describe individual experiences, are
        not typical or guaranteed results, and your results may differ.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>24. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, {legalName}, Dr. Robert Peterson, and our owners, employees,
        chapter leads, coaches, volunteers, and speakers will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special,
        consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of profits, revenue, data, or goodwill, arising out of or
        relating to your use of this website, the self-assessment, or your participation in {dbaName}{' '}
        activities. Where liability cannot be excluded, our total liability relating to this website is limited to one hundred
        United States dollars (USD 100).
      </p>
      <p class={`${bodyClass} mt-4`}>
        Nothing in these terms excludes or limits liability that cannot be excluded or limited under applicable law,
        including liability for gross negligence or willful misconduct. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain
        limitations of liability, so parts of this section may not apply to you.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>25. Indemnification</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {legalName}, Dr. Robert Peterson, and our owners, employees, chapter
        leads, coaches, volunteers, and speakers from any claims, losses, liabilities, and reasonable legal fees arising
        from your misuse of this website, your conduct at any {dbaName} activity, or your breach of these terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>26. Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The current version is always posted on this page with its
        effective date. Continued use of the site or participation in our activities after an update means you accept
        the revised terms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>27. Governing law and venue</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of {governingState}, without regard to its conflict of laws
        rules. Any dispute relating to these terms, this website, or {dbaName} activities will be brought in the state or
        federal courts located in {governingCounty} County, {governingState}, and you consent to the jurisdiction of
        those courts.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>28. General</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        If any provision of these terms is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions stay in effect. Our failure to
        enforce any provision is not a waiver of it. These terms, together with any participation agreement, membership
        terms, or other written agreement between us, form the entire agreement regarding their subject matter. Where a
        signed agreement conflicts with these terms, the signed agreement controls.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class={headingClass}>29. Contact</h2>
      <p class={bodyClass}>
        Questions about these terms can be sent to:<br /><br />
        {legalName}<br />
        {
          CONTACT.address.street && (
            <>
              {CONTACT.address.street}
              <br />
            </>
          )
        }
        {CONTACT.address.cityLine}
        {/* Email and phone hidden per request — restore when ready */}
        {false && CONTACT.email && (
          <>
            <br />
            Email: <a class={linkClass} href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>
          </>
        )}
        {
          CONTACT.phone.display && CONTACT.phone.href && (
            <>
              <br />
              Phone:{' '}
              <a class={linkClass} href={CONTACT.phone.href}>
                {CONTACT.phone.display}
              </a>
            </>
          )
        }
      </p>
    </section>
  </LegalDoc>
</Layout>
